The framework is meant to be adopted and adapted: copy the templates, drop the rules you
do not need, delete the sections you would never fill in. The one thing the license asks
in return, if you redistribute a modified version, is that you say you modified it
(§4.b), because anyone reading a set of rules needs to know whether they are reading
these or a variant of them.

Product Memory integration: this source distribution does not bundle third-party Python
packages, provider binaries, grammars or models. third_party/manifest.yaml records runtime
dependencies, their publisher license metadata and reviewed-but-not-copied sources;
third_party/inventory.json and constraints.txt are generated from that inventory.
The optional Enola executable is supplied separately by the operator. Redistributing it
or bundling Python packages is a separate distribution scope: preserve their respective
licenses/notices and review all bundled obligations. This notice is not a binary SBOM.
